  (text "COMPUTE MODULE on a 2 x 20 female header (J2, 2.54 mm, 8.5 mm insulator), Raspberry Pi 40-pin map (a Pi-compatible module: reference Radxa Zero 3W).\nPins 2 / 4: 5 V in from the buck (MOD_5V). GND pins 6, 9, 14, 20, 25, 30, 34, 39: AUX_GND. UART: pin 8 module TXD, pin 10 module RXD, to the ESP32 through 1k.\nPin 29 ALIVE (module out), 31 SHUTDOWN_REQ (module in), 33 ATTN (spare). Pins 1 / 17 (the module's 3.3 V) are not used. The ESP32 never drives\na line into a module that is off: 1k in series, and the firmware holds its outputs low while the buck is off." (at 300 20 0) (effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left top)) (uuid "288e6a8b-e754-5913-9c70-1c57f71d19ef"))
